          "en": "Interpretation of the Standing Committee of the National People's Congress\non Article 30 of the Criminal Law of the People's Republic of China\n(Adopted at the 8th meeting of the Standing Committee of the Twelfth National People's Congress on 24 April 2014)\nIn light of the situations encountered in judicial practice, the Standing Committee of the National People's Congress discussed the meaning of Article 30 of the Criminal Law and the question of how the relevant provisions of the Criminal Law apply where a company, an enterprise, a public institution, an organ, a body or any other unit commits an act endangering society as prescribed by the Criminal Law, but neither the Special Part of the Criminal Law nor other laws provide for the criminal responsibility of the unit, and gives the following interpretation:\nWhere a company, an enterprise, a public institution, an organ, a body or any other unit commits an act endangering society as prescribed by the Criminal Law, but neither the Special Part of the Criminal Law nor other laws provide for the criminal responsibility of the unit, the persons who organise, plan and carry out that act endangering society shall be investigated for criminal responsibility in accordance with law.\nIt is hereby announced."
