        "no": 79,
        "text": {
          "en": "Interpretation of Paragraph 3 of Article 79 of the Criminal Procedure Law of the People's Republic of China\n(Adopted at the 8th meeting of the Standing Committee of the Twelfth National People's Congress on 24 April 2014)\nIn light of the situations encountered in judicial practice, the Standing Committee of the National People's Congress discussed the question of whether the provision of Paragraph 3 of Article 79 of the Criminal Procedure Law, under which arrest may be approved where the provisions on release on bail pending trial or on residential surveillance are seriously violated, applies to a criminal suspect or defendant who may be sentenced to a penalty not heavier than fixed-term imprisonment, and gives the following interpretation:\nIn accordance with the provisions of Paragraph 3 of Article 79 of the Criminal Procedure Law, where a criminal suspect or defendant who is released on bail pending trial or under residential surveillance and who may be sentenced to a penalty not heavier than fixed-term imprisonment violates the provisions on release on bail pending trial or on residential surveillance and thereby seriously affects the normal conduct of the proceedings, arrest may be approved.\nIt is hereby announced."
        },
